# SQL's `NOT LIKE` with `%x%`: DS0105 suggesting `!contains`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT LIKE '%42%'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..48
  PIPELINE@0..47
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..47
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..47
        NAME_REF@21..31
          IDENT@21..31 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        IDENT@32..35 "NOT"
        WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
        IDENT@36..40 "LIKE"
        WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
        LITERAL@41..47
          STRING@41..47 "'%42%'"
  WHITESPACE@47..48 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `NOT LIKE` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:33
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where customerId NOT LIKE '%42%'
  |                                 ^^^^^^^^ this is SQL's pattern match
  |
  = help: use `!contains`: `customerId !contains '42'`
  = note: `contains` ignores case; `contains_cs` matches case exactly
